sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Human adopter
    participant RI as Repository intelligence
    participant Init as Brownfield init
    participant Upgrade as Managed upgrade
    participant Adapter as Layout compatibility
    participant Tx as Managed transaction
    participant Adopt as Adoption evidence
    participant Review as Human adaptation and validation

    rect rgb(232, 245, 233)
    User->>RI: Plan baseline repository intelligence
    RI->>RI: Inspect source, tests, docs, specs, CI, and relationships
    RI-->>User: Immutable plan, findings, component recommendation, digest
    alt Repository intelligence is applicable
        User->>RI: Enroll exact scope, re-plan, digest-confirm apply, validate
        RI-->>User: Source-bound SQLite/FTS generation and receipts
    else Not applicable for the executed repository
        RI-->>User: Explicit not-applicable evidence; no component installed
    end
    end
    Note over User,RI: NetworkX/GraphML is selected only when the executed relationship model adds value.<br/>sqlite-vec remains off until a deterministic vector workload exists.<br/>Profile and declared L0-L5 maturity guide review; neither grants approval.

    rect rgb(227, 242, 253)
    User->>Init: Preview Standard or Assured brownfield activation
    Init->>Adapter: Check prospective setup destinations and existing host-owned Python namespaces
    alt Host owns scripts/ and setup could later add Python there
        Adapter->>Adapter: Remap exact NAOS tool paths to naos_tools/
        Adapter-->>Init: Rewritten setup catalogue, Makefile, workflow, hook, and surface contract
    else No blocking namespace collision
        Adapter-->>Init: Keep normal generated layout
    end
    Init-->>User: Complete no-target-mutation preview and bounded compatibility report
    User->>Init: Separate reviewed --activate invocation
    Init->>Tx: Bind repository-intelligence generation and managed-content plan
    Tx->>Tx: Lock, stage, journal, publish each leaf atomically, receipt, recover on interruption
    Tx-->>User: Specs 01-10, task registry, dashboard seed, rules, controls, and provenance
    end
    Note over Init,Tx: Existing adopter files are preserved. Any destination collision refuses the whole create-only activation.<br/>The layout adapter changes only the generated preview before the transaction digest is frozen.

    rect rgb(255, 248, 225)
    User->>Adopt: Run brownfield adoption against the installed surface
    Adopt->>Adopt: Inventories, baseline, candidate requirements, gaps, challenges, decision record
    Adopt-->>Review: Deterministic reports; activation_planned remains false
    Review->>Review: Accept, reject, defer, or edit candidates into project-owned specs and tasks
    Review->>Review: Run gov-refresh, dashboard, profile and maturity gates, and native tests
    Review-->>User: Evidence-backed onboarding result with remaining gaps stated
    end
    Note over Adopt,Review: Candidate evidence is never promoted automatically.<br/>Initial installation remains create-only; later upgrades preserve human edits.

    rect rgb(255, 235, 238)
    User->>Upgrade: Plan later managed profile transition
    Upgrade->>Upgrade: Classify complete base / current / new inventory
    Upgrade-->>User: External immutable plan, preservation decisions, SHA-256 digest
    User->>Upgrade: Apply exact plan with expected digest
    Upgrade->>Upgrade: Regenerate fixed sources and revalidate provenance and current state
    Upgrade->>Tx: Replace only unchanged kit-owned derived regular files
    Tx->>Tx: Journal, ordered atomic leaves, receipt; rollback or recover on interruption
    Tx-->>User: Applied, refused, recovery-required, or rollback-incomplete result
    end
    Note over Upgrade,Tx: Adopter-owned, modified, ambiguous, unsafe, and out-of-scope content is preserved.<br/>Managed init transitions and eligible add/setup collisions use this same service; blanket force is refused.<br/>Mutation support is the executed Darwin regular-file adapter only.

    rect rgb(243, 229, 245)
    Note over User,RI: Controlled comparison: Repo 1 uses the SQLite/FTS baseline.<br/>Only after Repo 1 completes, Repo 2 starts from an identical source copy and adds NetworkX/GraphML.<br/>Graph expansion may reprioritize human review but cannot change candidate authority, confidence, or promotion state.<br/>Compare coverage, accuracy, manual work, runtime, preservation, and native-test results before claiming benefit.
    end
